Package: popcomp
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Count Models for Population-Referenced Compositions
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Mohammed", "Sabri", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "mohammed.sabri@kaust.edu.sa",
    comment = c(affiliation = "King Abdullah University of Science and Technology (KAUST), Saudi Arabia"))
Description: Fits Bayesian count models for the composition of cases over ordered
    categories (for example age groups), relative to a reference distribution
    (for example the population age structure), through the multinomial-Poisson
    transformation with diffuse Gaussian row intercepts in R-INLA, approximating
    conditional multinomial inference. Covariates act on an orthonormal basis over the
    categories, with spatial (BYM2) and cell-level overdispersion effects.
    Contrasts in the mean and the Wasserstein-1 distance between predicted
    compositions are computed as posterior functionals, marginal over the
    random effects or for a typical unit, and summarised with tolerance
    (near-null) probabilities.
